{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "forcing_gated_overlap_regrid",
    "description": "A gated conservative overlap regrid (join.overlap on ring envelopes plus a sliver filter A_ij > 1e-12, the conservative_overlap_*_gated template shape) whose source field F is data-fed, so it is a forcing slot of the program and the gated apply must read it from the forcing set on every call. F is a 1 x 3 loader field read through a flattened cell-to-row reindex, PHI[c] = F[floor((c-1)/3)+1, c-3 floor((c-1)/3)] (1 + 0.1 src_poly[c,1,1]), as reseact's NEI emissions read theirs. The regridded field F_tgt is spread over a 3-level column with a surface-only ifelse (Fm) and drives D(u[j,k]) = Fm[j,k] - kd u[j,k]. Source cells: unit squares at x = 0, 1.5, 3; targets [0,2] and [3.5,4.5]; surviving overlaps (1,1) = 1, (2,1) = 0.5, (3,2) = 0.5. Issue #665: Julia rhs_program used to refuse this under native. The ring pitch and the sliver tolerance are literals, not parameters: the Problem's reference fills its per-refresh cache with the parameters it was built with, while the program reads p on every call.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST test suite"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "public_rhs_program"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "src_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "tgt_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "verts": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "coord": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "fr": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    },
    "fc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    }
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "Src": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "{unused_placeholder}"
      }
    }
  },
